  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to break in; to force one's way in; to burst in",
      "explanation": "Used for unauthorized entry, often with criminal or aggressive implications. Intransitive verb formed from 押す (to push) + 入る (to enter)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06760_oshiiru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{強盗|ごうとう}が{家|いえ}に{押|お}し{入|い}った。",
      "english": "A robber broke into the house.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06760_oshiiru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{不審者|ふしんしゃ}が{店|みせ}に{押|お}し{入|い}り、{現金|げんきん}を{奪|うば}った。",
      "english": "A suspicious person broke into the store and stole cash.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06760_oshiiru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{警察|けいさつ}が{容疑者|ようぎしゃ}の{部屋|へや}に{押|お}し{入|い}った。",
      "english": "The police forced their way into the suspect's room.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{押|お}し{入|い}る is an intransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}) formed from {押|お}す (to push) + {入|い}る (to enter).\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n・[place]に{押|お}し{入|い}る - to break into [place]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{家|いえ}に{押|お}し{入|い}る - to break into a house\n・{店|みせ}に{押|お}し{入|い}る - to break into a store\n・{強盗|ごうとう}が{押|お}し{入|い}る - a robber breaks in\n\nRELATED:\n・{押|お}し{込|こ}む - to force into\n・{侵入|しんにゅう}する - to intrude (more formal)",
